   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **It Beats for You**: back after 30 archived shows (906 days) [5]\n- **That Way He Sings**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Losin' Yo Head**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **Friends Again**: rare: 5 archived performances [5]\n- **End of Run**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Move on Up**: rare: 10 archived performances [5]\n- **Mother In Law**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Carnival Time**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Carried Away [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2010-04-21.mmj2010-04-21.flac** (recommended): source not stated; 25 songs; 146 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **mmj2010-04-21.mk4v-mk41.flac24**: source not stated; 25 songs; 146 min [2]\n- **mmj2010-04-21.mk4v-mk41.flac16**: source not stated; 25 songs; 146 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Preservation Hall Jazz Band joined the band for songs from Evil Urges through Carnival Time [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2010-04-21.mmj2010-04-21.flac**: taped by willsfc; transferred by MSTaper; source: Avantone CK1 > Fostex FR-2LE [1]. Also: Recorded by willSFC using an MSTaper Jr., positioned near the front of the stage; Audio captured via Avantone CK1 mics into a Fostex FR-2LE recorder [1]\n- **mmj2010-04-21.mk4v-mk41.flac24**: taped by Taylor Caine; transferred by taylorc; source: [24bit] Schoeps mk4v> KCY> Schoeps VMS02IB + Schoeps mk41> KC5> M222> NT222> Lunatec V3> SD 744t (@24bit/96kHz) [2]\n- **mmj2010-04-21.mk4v-mk41.flac16**: taped by Taylor Caine; transferred by taylorc; source: [16bit] Schoeps mk4v> KCY> Schoeps VMS02IB + Schoeps mk41> KC5> M222> NT222> Lunatec V3> SD 744t (@24bit/96kHz) [3]",
